id: tased
name: Tased
kind: conditions
# One stack per clock, so the hold lasts until the last Taser's clock runs out rather than
# the first. The cap only has to be out of anybody's reach.
maxStacks: 99
# Not a Combat Condition: the entry names Prone, and this is only what keeps it on.
combatCondition: no
# The Combat Condition this mark keeps from being removed while it is held. Read by
# `setCondition`, which names no mark.
holds: prone
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Still jolted by a Taser. You cannot get up from Prone yet.
text: >
  Tased: the Taser's mark. "They cannot remove the Prone Combat Condition inflicted by a
  Taser until then."

---

# The rule stops a Condition coming off rather than going on - Guard Down in a Grapple is the
# other one like it - so it is held where removals are refused, and the mark is what says so.
#
# Gained before the Prone and on the same clock, so it runs out first: the Prone's own clock
# then finds nothing holding it, and it comes off when the entry says it does.
#
# No effects of its own.
